To assess the impact of each component on the performance of R$^{2}$-LLMs, we conducted a series of ablation experiments. The baseline MCTS method is compared against three variants: MCTS$_\text{w/DLR}$, which incorporates logical reasoning enhancements, MCTS$_\text{w/FG}$, which integrates fine-grained enhancement, and MCTS$_\text{w/DLR+FG}$ is equal to R$^{2}$-LLMs, which combines both improvements.

