\section{Results and Analysis}\label{sec:results}

This section presents a comprehensive analysis of EvoSort’s performance, emphasizing how the proposed GA dynamically tunes critical parameters to optimize sorting time. We discuss the GA convergence, parameter evolution, and final performance comparisons for datasets of sizes $10^7$, $10^8$, $5\times10^8$, $10^9$, $5\times10^9$, and $10^{10}$ elements. Finally, we provide a detailed comparison table summarizing execution times and speedup factors.

For each dataset size, the GA starts with a population (typically 30 individuals) that explores various combinations of these parameters. Over approximately 10 generations, the GA applies uniform recombination  (with probability 0.7) and uniform mutation (with probability 0.3) while preserving the best individuals via elitism \citep{Holland1975,Goldberg1989,Mitchell1996,Deb2001,Deb2002}. 

\subsection{Performance Comparison Across Data Sizes}

After the GA converges for a given dataset, the optimized parameters are applied to the full sorting routine. The following subsections describe the final execution times and speedup factors for each dataset size, while explaining the whole optimization process for each dataset.

