As shown in the figure, the GA quickly reduces the average sorting time from over 6.6\,s in Generation~0 to around 0.24\,s by Generation~2. Beyond that point, the best solutions remain clustered near 0.24--0.29\,s, indicating that the GA has already found a near-optimal configuration. This rapid convergence is a hallmark of evolutionary algorithms when applied to well-defined performance objectives \citep{Goldberg1989,Mitchell1996}.

\vspace{1ex}
\paragraph*{Key Observations from the GA Process:}
\begin{itemize}
    \item \textbf{Initial Population Diversity:} In Generation~0, the GA evaluates a wide range of parameter combinations, leading to execution times spanning from 6.6247\,s (a relatively poor configuration) down to 0.2416\,s (an unexpectedly strong early discovery).
