\section{Objectives}
The main objectives of this tutorial are as follows:
\begin{itemize}[leftmargin=*]
    \item \textbf{Introduce the Dynamic RAG Paradigm:} Attendees will gain a solid understanding of Dynamic Retrieval-Augmented Generation, which enables retrieval to occur adaptively during the generation process. 
    The tutorial will highlight three key challenges in this field: when to retrieve, what to retrieve, and how to inject knowledge. 
    This foundation will help attendees grasp the motivations and core mechanisms behind Dynamic RAG.



    \item \textbf{Introduce How to Address the Real-time Information Needs of LLMs:} 
    Participants will learn practical methods for detecting an LLM’s information needs during generation, such as uncertainty-based retrieval triggering mechanisms and dynamic query formulation. 


    \item \textbf{Introduce Parametric Knowledge Injection Strategies:} 
    We will introduce recent advances in knowledge injection, including Parametric RAG, which integrates knowledge directly into model parameters. This section contrasts parametric and in-context approaches, helping attendees understand their respective advantages in terms of performance and efficiency.





    \item \textbf{Encourage Future Research Directions:} 
    The tutorial will conclude by discussing open challenges and promising directions in Dynamic RAG. By bridging Information Retrieval and LLM research, we aim to inspire new approaches to building adaptive, retrieval-aware generative systems.

\end{itemize}

