The following theorem highlights a notable property of transitive orientation when applied to cliques.

\begin{theorem}
\cite{kitaev2021word} Let \( K_m \) be a clique on \(m\) vertices in a graph \( G \). Then, any acyclic orientation of \( G \) induces a transitive orientation on \( K_m \). In particular, every semi-transitive orientation of \( G \) yields a transitive orientation on \( K_m \). Moreover, in both cases, the induced orientation on \( K_m \) contains exactly one source and one sink (as shown in Figure \ref{km}).
\end{theorem}



